mutant: m069_sync_state_promoted_after_append
target: internal/ingest/live/consumer.go
failure-mode: |
  Verifier sync state is promoted after Append returns instead of in the
  writer's OnAppend hook for the event's last row (the S2.18 fix, see
  specs/oracle/2026-09-25-disagg-syncstate-batch-boundary.md). A batch cut
  between the append and the promotion holds the rows without their chain
  state; if the leader dies before the next batch commits, the event is
  redelivered and archived twice.
expected-detection: |
  TestConsumer_Hot_ChainStateCommitsWithLastRow cuts a batch at exactly
  that point. The layer 3 oracle found the bug on full seeds 1, 2, 3, 5
  and 6 (a whole event archived twice), but that depends on a batch cut
  landing in the gap, so the unit test is the reliable executioner.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

diff --git a/internal/ingest/live/consumer.go b/internal/ingest/live/consumer.go
